### =============================================
### BULK ORDER PROCESSING COMPREHENSIVE DEMO
### =============================================
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates parent-child workflow patterns and parallel processing
### AUDIENCE: Perfect for showcasing advanced workflow orchestration capabilities
### SCENARIOS: Covers bulk orders, child workflows, and approval patterns
### MONITORING: Real-time notifications for parent and child workflow tracking
### DURATION: Allow 5-10 minutes for full demonstration
### =============================================

### =============================================
### PHASE 1: SYSTEM PREPARATION
### =============================================

### 1. Health check for batch processor service
### Expected: Service should be running and healthy
GET http://localhost:3007/health

### 2. Check inventory levels before bulk processing
### Expected: Sufficient stock for demonstration orders
GET http://localhost:3013/api/v1/inventory

### 3. Restock inventory if needed for demonstration
### Purpose: Ensure sufficient stock for bulk order processing
POST http://localhost:3013/api/v1/inventory/restock

### =============================================
### PHASE 2: STANDARD BULK ORDER PROCESSING
### =============================================

### 4. Submit a standard bulk order with multiple items
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates parent workflow spawning child workflows
### MONITORING: Watch notifications UI (localhost:8080) for [BULK] prefixed messages
### EXPECTED: Parent workflow creates child workflows for each item
// @name bulkorder
POST http://localhost:3007/bulk-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": "alice",
  "items": [
    {"item": "apple", "quantity": 2, "price": 50.0},
    {"item": "orange", "quantity": 1, "price": 75.0},
    {"item": "pear", "quantity": 3, "price": 30.0}
  ]
}

### 5. Get bulk order status and child workflow IDs
### PURPOSE: Monitor parent workflow and track child workflow creation
### EXPECTED: Response shows parent status and list of child workflow instances
@bulk_instance_id = {{bulkorder.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3007/bulk-orders/{{bulk_instance_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 3: HIGH-VALUE BULK ORDER (APPROVAL WORKFLOW)
### =============================================

### 6. Submit a bulk order with expensive items (triggers approval workflow)
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates approval workflow integration with bulk processing
### MONITORING: Watch for approval requirement notifications
### EXPECTED: Items over $500 require approval via external events
// @name bulkorder_expensive
POST http://localhost:3007/bulk-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": "bob",
  "items": [
    {"item": "kiwi", "quantity": 1, "price": 800.0},
    {"item": "apple", "quantity": 2, "price": 600.0}
  ]
}

### 7. Get expensive bulk order status (check for approval requirements)
### PURPOSE: Verify which child workflows require approval
### EXPECTED: High-value items show pending approval status
@bulk_expensive_instance_id = {{bulkorder_expensive.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3007/bulk-orders/{{bulk_expensive_instance_id}}

### 8. Approve a specific high-value item in the bulk order
### PURPOSE: Demonstrate external event handling for child workflows
### NOTE: Replace with actual child workflow ID from bulk order response
### FORMAT: bulk_{customer}_{suffix}_child_{index}_{item}
### EXPECTED: Approved item proceeds with processing, others remain pending
POST http://localhost:3007/bulk-orders/bulk_bob_3gu2ao/items/bulk_bob_3gu2ao_child_1_apple/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approver": "manager",
  "approved": true
}

### =============================================
### PHASE 4: BULK ORDER VARIANTS FOR TESTING
### =============================================

### 9. Submit a mixed-value bulk order (some items need approval)
### PURPOSE: Test combination of standard and high-value items
### MONITORING: Observe differential processing paths
// @name mixed_bulk_order
POST http://localhost:3007/bulk-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": "charlie",
  "items": [
    {"item": "apple", "quantity": 3, "price": 45.0},
    {"item": "kiwi", "quantity": 1, "price": 750.0},
    {"item": "orange", "quantity": 2, "price": 35.0}
  ]
}

### 10. Submit a single-item bulk order (edge case testing)
### PURPOSE: Test bulk processing with minimal complexity
### EXPECTED: Still creates parent-child workflow pattern
// @name single_item_bulk
POST http://localhost:3007/bulk-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": "diana",
  "items": [
    {"item": "pear", "quantity": 5, "price": 25.0}
  ]
}

### 11. Get mixed bulk order status
### PURPOSE: Monitor complex approval scenarios
@mixed_bulk_instance_id = {{mixed_bulk_order.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3007/bulk-orders/{{mixed_bulk_instance_id}}

### 12. Get single-item bulk order status
### PURPOSE: Verify edge case handling
@single_bulk_instance_id = {{single_item_bulk.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3007/bulk-orders/{{single_bulk_instance_id}}

### =============================================
### BULK ORDER WORKFLOW DEMONSTRATION POINTS
### =============================================
###
### 🎯 KEY FEATURES TO HIGHLIGHT:
###
### 1. PARENT-CHILD WORKFLOW ORCHESTRATION:
###    - Single bulk order creates multiple child workflows
###    - Each item processed independently with parallel execution
###    - Parent workflow coordinates and tracks all children
###    - Clear activity names for workflow visualization
###
### 2. ADVANCED ACTIVITY NAMING:
###    - announce_bulk_order_started: Clear workflow initiation
###    - announce_child_workflow_spawned: Track child creation
###    - announce_waiting_for_children: Parent coordination point
###    - announce_item_success/failure: Individual outcomes
###    - announce_inventory_reserved: Business logic completion
###    - announce_payment_processing: Payment stage identification
###    - announce_shipping_scheduled: Final fulfillment step
###
### 3. REAL-TIME MONITORING:
###    - Live notifications with [BULK] prefix in UI
###    - Parent and child workflow status tracking
###    - Progress updates for each processing stage
###    - Failure isolation between child workflows
###
### 4. APPROVAL WORKFLOW INTEGRATION:
###    - Automatic approval detection for high-value items
###    - External event handling for manager approvals
###    - Individual item approval within bulk orders
###    - Timeout handling for pending approvals
###
### 5. PARALLEL PROCESSING BENEFITS:
###    - Multiple items processed simultaneously
###    - Inventory reservation coordination
###    - Payment processing optimization
###    - Shipping schedule coordination
###
### 6. FAILURE HANDLING:
###    - Graceful handling of partial bulk order failures
###    - Individual item failure isolation
###    - Compensation patterns for failed items
###    - Parent workflow status aggregation
###
### 7. SCALABILITY DEMONSTRATION:
###    - Bulk orders of varying sizes (1-10+ items)
###    - Mixed-value scenarios with differential processing
###    - Resource efficient child workflow spawning
###    - Coordinated completion handling
###
### =============================================
### 🚀 DEMO EXECUTION GUIDE:
###
### TIMING: Execute requests with 10-15 second delays for observation
### MONITORING: Keep notifications UI (localhost:8080) open during demo
### OBSERVATION: Watch for parent workflow coordination messages
### ANALYSIS: Use workflow IDs to trace parent-child relationships
### APPROVAL: Use actual child workflow IDs from bulk order responses
###
### EXPECTED DEMO DURATION: 5-10 minutes for complete demonstration
### CONCURRENT PROCESSING: Child workflows execute in parallel
### NOTIFICATION RATE: Expect 5-15 events per bulk order
### =============================================
